    "updated_at": "2026-05-27T06:34:53Z",
    "body": "I think browsers might already use the first `legend` element child instead of the first element child if that happens to be a `legend` element. I suspect this needs some demos/tests to demonstrate where browsers are not behaving in these non-conforming scenarios as you would expect and then we can see if that is something we want to change or not. Or perhaps they already behave as you want in which case this is a conformance question.",
