    "created_at": "2026-06-01T14:09:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-01T14:09:19Z",
    "body": "I think we shouldn't change this to allow for descendant `legend` because that would make it harder to use `legend` for other purposes. We already have `legend` in `optgroup`, so this would use \"foo\" as the `fieldset`'s legend if it used the first descendant `legend`:\n\n```html\n<fieldset>\n <select>\n  <optgroup>\n   <legend>foo</legend>\n  </optgroup>\n </select>\n</fieldset>\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/4593368372/reactions",
